  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "This is the hard version of TOOFAREZ, and is worth 606060 points. Note that the input formats of both problems differ slightly - in particular, this version has an additional array AAA as input.\n\nAn array AAA of length MMM is said to be prefix-balanced under the following conditions:\n\n\nLet SAS_ASA​ denote the set of all elements that appear in AAA.\nFor each x∈SAx \\in S_Ax∈SA​, and index iii (1≤i≤M1 \\leq i \\leq M1≤i≤M), let fi(x)f_i(x)fi​(x) denote the number of times xxx appears among [A1,A2,…,Ai][A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_i][A1​,A2​,…,Ai​].\n\nThat is, fi(x)f_i(x)fi​(x) denotes the frequency of xxx in AAA's prefix of length iii.\nThen, AAA is called prefix-balanced if, for **every** triple of integers (x,y,i)(x, y, i)(x,y,i) such that x,y∈SAx, y \\in S_Ax,y∈SA​ and 1≤i≤M1 \\leq i \\leq M1≤i≤M, we have\n\n∣fi(x)−fi(y)∣≤1|f_i(x) - f_i(y)| \\leq 1∣fi​(x)−fi​(y)∣≤1\nFor example, the arrays [1,2,1][1, 2, 1][1,2,1] and [1,3,2,3][1, 3, 2, 3][1,3,2,3] are prefix-balanced, but [2,3,2,4][2, 3, 2, 4][2,3,2,4] is not (the prefix of length 333 contains two occurrences of 222 and no occurrences of 444).\n\nYou are given an array AAA of length NNN, and an integer MMM.\n\nEvery element of AAA lies between 000 and MMM.\n\nLet KKK denote the number of zeros in AAA. There are MKM^KMK arrays that can be obtained by replacing every 000 in AAA with an integer between 111 and MMM.\n\nHow many of these MKM^KMK arrays are prefix-balanced?\n\nThe answer might be large, so find it modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and MMM — the length of the array and the maximum allowed value.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ — the elements of array AAA.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the number of ways of replacing the zeros in AAA, such that the resulting array is prefix-balanced, modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤5⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 5\\cdot 10^51≤N≤5⋅105",
      "1≤M≤5⋅1051 \\leq M \\leq 5\\cdot 10^51≤M≤5⋅105",
      "0≤Ai≤M0 \\leq A_i \\leq M0≤Ai​≤M",
      "The sum of NNN and the sum of MMM over all test cases won't exceed 5⋅1055\\cdot 10^55⋅105."
    ],
